# secure-shell toast.surface — a wish, as a window.
# The first payload served over the upgraded contract (`tools/port/served.mjs`):
# the server mounts this surface, receipts it with `surface.mount/2`, and serves
# the window record plus its evidence rows. The client never learns a package tag.
#
# Lane `beacon` and rule `small-right` are the vendored tables' own
# (`tools/port/surface.mjs`); no lane or rule is added here. A toast carries no
# chrome and no moves: nothing about it can be minimized, and it is not dragged.
dl-enclave.surface/1
surface	secure-shell-toast
requires	observe
window	toast	Wish	beacon	small-right	0	0	36	5	28	4	false	false			surface	toast-wish
node	toast	toast-root	-	pane	surface	-
node	toast	toast-wish	toast-root	label	surface	$wish
